00:07:42,540 --> 00:07:52,620
 Um, so pivotally, the thing that I mentioned that it communicates, obviously protocol version and client info are important, but not quite as much, um, as capabilities, okay.

68
00:07:52,620 --> 00:08:02,820
 Um, capabilities, uh, lets the server know what kind of, um, uh, well, capabilities the client has access to.

69
00:08:03,180 --> 00:08:05,620
 Um, and there are three options currently defined in the spec.

70
00:08:05,620 --> 00:08:09,260
 Roots, sampling and elicitation, and we'll cover all of those later.

71
00:08:09,260 --> 00:08:15,900
 Um, there's also a subscribe and list changed, um, attribute beneath the capabilities for each one of these.

72
00:08:15,900 --> 00:08:19,500
 So, you know, roots, list changed, true, subscribe, true.

73
00:08:19,500 --> 00:08:23,260
 Um, and that supports whether, uh, you can get notifications, et cetera.

74
00:08:24,660 --> 00:08:37,540
 Okay, so, you know, if you're an NPC, uh, MC, um, MCP server, you're going to receive a JSON RPC from the client, and it's going to contain some set of capabilities, the protocol version and the client info.

75
00:08:37,660 --> 00:08:38,060
 Cool.

76
00:08:38,060 --> 00:08:47,780
 Now as the, uh, MCP server, you're going to respond, uh, and give them your capabilities, your protocol version, your server info, and then also your instructions.

