00:13:21,420 --> 00:13:40,420
 The model context protocol provides a standardized way for clients to expose file system roots to the server. Hell yes. That is exactly what we want. Um, and clients that support roots must declare those roots during, uh, initialization in the compatibilities, uh, section.

